Description: An R toolkit for plant- and animal-breeding genotype workflows:
    convert CSV and HapMap genotype tables to VCF, validate and repair VCFs
    for Beagle, run Beagle imputation and phasing from R, and capture
    structured run records. Simulate linked breeding genotypes conditional
    on phased founder haplotypes and genetic maps using explicit diploid
    and random-bivalent autotetraploid inheritance models.
    Beagle and PLINK are external command-line tools
    invoked from R; the package focuses on preprocessing and imputation,
    not downstream analyses.
